WEBVTT

00:00:04.940 --> 00:00:11.730
The deep ocean;  a place so different
filled with strange life-forms.  But

00:00:11.730 --> 00:00:18.410
what's down there?  How much do we know
about it?  As it turns out, not very much.

00:00:18.410 --> 00:00:25.220
95% of the ocean remains unexplored.  Most
of which is considered the deep ocean.

00:00:25.220 --> 00:00:29.590
But what exactly is the deep ocean?

00:00:29.590 --> 00:00:35.720
The first 200 meters of the ocean are
the open ocean.  Much of the marine life

00:00:35.720 --> 00:00:39.760
we know of lives here where there is
light.

00:00:40.480 --> 00:00:47.670
Below 200 meters where there is little
light left, you enter the twilight zone

00:00:47.940 --> 00:00:53.800
Once you pass 1000 meters the water is
completely devoid of light and you have

00:00:53.800 --> 00:01:00.850
reached the deep ocean.  Down here
temperatures plummet to 39 degrees

00:01:00.850 --> 00:01:05.920
Fahrenheit and constantly stay near
freezing.  The pressures at these depths

00:01:05.920 --> 00:01:10.000
range from about 40 to over a hundred
and ten times the pressure of Earth's

00:01:10.000 --> 00:01:19.660
atmosphere.  But how could anything thrive
in these conditions.  It was originally

00:01:19.660 --> 00:01:24.460
thought that life cannot survive without
light.  We now know that despite this lack

00:01:24.460 --> 00:01:29.500
of light, many creatures can live in this
extreme place, such as microorganisms in

00:01:29.500 --> 00:01:38.050
hydrothermal vents,
deep sea corals, fish and many other

00:01:38.050 --> 00:01:46.690
bizarre creatures.  Exploring the deep
ocean is challenging because of the

00:01:46.690 --> 00:01:50.980
harsh conditions but marine scientists
are on a mission to document new species

00:01:50.980 --> 00:01:57.560
in this unusual place.

00:02:00.140 --> 00:02:02.200
 

